Yeah, I like this. I think some gods (the violent, aggressive ones of
the wombat classes) should be more likely to blast the enemy, while
more peaceful Gods (ie healer, priest Gods, maybe rangers) should be
more likely to offer healing in times of need. Giving the assorted
deities more individual behaviour would give the various classes a bit
more character and differentiation.

It also makes the game a little more difficult for certain classes: ie
barbarians, valkyries: After all, you can think of being surrounded by
monsters and low on hit points as two seperate problems:
1) surrounded by monsters
2) low on hitpoints.
Wombat characters are good at dealing with problem 1 (ie, they are good
at killing stuff) but less equipped to deal with problem 2 (ie they are
less likely to have the means for healing themselves). Healers, priests
etc are the opposite: They can deal with 2 far more easily than 1.
As the game currently stands, a wombat's God will help out with the
problem they are less able to deal with themselves (the HP), leaving
them to casually mop up the monsters once healed. They get the best of
both worlds. On the other hand a healer's god will help out wth the
thing they could do for themselves anyway (healing), and leave them
surrounded by nasties that will just strip those HP right back down
again. This is probably one of the reasons (though not the only reason
by any means) barbs and valks seem to be more ascendable than healers
and priests.

So, making the Barbarian and valk gods act a little more "in character"
by blasting the enemies to ash but leaving the player with dismally low
HP might redress the balance a little bit.

Also, I would propose a third alternative to healing and zapping:
Paralyse the enemy/ enemies. This might be more appropriate for
healers, whose Gods ought to abhor bloodshed. It would also be more
in-character for pacifist players, so if a character has maintained
pacifist conduct so far, any helpful divine lightning should be
substituted for temporary paralysis.


